@startuml

title Game end and new game

participant Client1
participant Server
participant Client2
database "Leaderboard DB\n(SQLite)" as DB

Client1->Server: last action of the final round\n(ChooseCardRequest / PassRequest)
Server->Server: resolve final events and end-game building effects
Server->Server: calculate winner(s) by prestige, then food

note right of Server
The END_GAME status and the winners are carried
inside the game snapshot (PlayerSummary.isWinner),
not as a dedicated message.
end note

group persist match results (once per finished game)
Server->Server: build finished snapshot (first time finished() is true)
loop each player in the game
Server->DB: saveMatchResult(nickname, prestige, timestamp, numPlayers)
end
DB-->Server: rows inserted
end

Server-->Client1: GameViewUpdate(finished snapshot)
Server-->Client2: GameViewUpdate(finished snapshot)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(final snapshot)

group show leaderboard on game end
note over Client1, Client2
On a finished snapshot the GUI fetches the leaderboard
automatically; the CLI fetches it on the "rank" command.
Each client does this independently.
end note

Client1->Server: RankingsRequest(gameName)
Server->DB: getLeaderboardByNumPlayers(numPlayers)
DB-->Server: top scores for that player count
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(rankings)
Client1->Client1: render leaderboard

Client2->Server: RankingsRequest(gameName)
Server->DB: getLeaderboardByNumPlayers(numPlayers)
DB-->Server: top scores for that player count
Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult(rankings)
Client2->Client2: render leaderboard
end

group leave the finished game
Client1->Server: UnsubscribeGameRequest
Server->Server: remove update sink and finished-game membership
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(subscription disabled)

Client2->Server: UnsubscribeGameRequest
Server->Server: remove update sink and finished-game membership
Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult(subscription disabled)
end

group return to lobby and start again
Client1->Server: LobbyRequest
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(joinable games)

alt create another game
Client1->Server: CreateGameRequest
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(Game created)
else join another game
Client1->Server: JoinGameRequest
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(Player joined)
end
end

note over Client1, Client2
Natural victories may be shared when prestige and food are tied.
A forced disconnection victory has one winner.
Rankings can be read only while the finished session still exists;
once every player has left, the session and its rankings are gone.
end note

@enduml
